            <div xml:id="d130">

                <pb facs="0280" n="152" sameAs="frus:frus1928v01/pg152"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.0012Anti-War/281: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Herrick</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-08-18T16:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 18,
                                1928—4 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>283. Your No. 248, August 18, 4 p.m. Department thought that France would not
                    have any objection to Morocco’s adherence, but instead would welcome it. As it
                    appears that objection does exist, the Department does not at this time desire
                    to push matter further. You may so inform the Foreign Office.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Castle</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
